# Citation metadata for the TCKDB software.
#
# This file describes how to cite the *software*. A curated scientific
# *dataset release* is a separate, independently citable artifact with its own
# immutable, checksummed manifest served at
#   GET /api/v1/scientific/releases/{tag}/manifest
# and its own citation string in `dataset_release.citation_text`. Cite the
# dataset when you use TCKDB's numbers; cite the software when you use or
# extend the code. See backend/docs/specs/dataset_release_and_profiles.md.
#
# `doi:` is intentionally absent. TCKDB does not mint DOIs speculatively — a
# DOI is not retractable, and the corpus is not yet published. The procedure
# for minting one when a paper tag is cut is documented in
# backend/docs/deployment/cutting_a_dataset_release.md.
#
# The same split runs through licensing, and CFF 1.2.0 has nowhere to put the
# second half of it. `license:` below is MIT: it describes *this software*.
# The scientific data is licensed separately under CC BY 4.0 — see
# `LICENSE-DATA` at the repository root for what that covers and what it does
# not, and `dataset_release.data_license` for the license a specific release
# was actually published under.
#
# `license:` accepts a list, so `[MIT, CC-BY-4.0]` would validate. It is not
# used, because it would be false: it says one work is available under either
# license, and TCKDB is two works under one each. `license-url:` is defined
# only for licenses absent from the SPDX list, and CC-BY-4.0 is on it. So the
# data license lives in prose here and in `LICENSE-DATA` in full — a reader
# who needs to cite the numbers reaches the dataset release anyway, which
# names its own license in the manifest it is cited by.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TCKDB — Thermochemical and Kinetics Database"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  If you use data obtained from a TCKDB instance, please additionally cite
  the specific dataset release (tag and manifest checksum) you queried.
  The software is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE); the scientific data is
  licensed separately under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA), which makes that
  citation an obligation of reuse, not only a courtesy.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pieters
    given-names: Calvin
  - family-names: Grinberg Dana
    given-names: Alon
    affiliation: "Technion – Israel Institute of Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TCKDB/TCKDB"
abstract: >-
  A provenance-rich, workflow-tool-agnostic database and HTTP API for
  computational and experimental chemistry data: species, reactions,
  transition states, geometries, calculations, statistical mechanics,
  thermochemistry, kinetics, transport, pressure-dependent networks, raw
  artifacts, and review state. Scientific records are append-only; curation
  is an overlay that never mutates the underlying values. Reads are served
  under an explicit exploratory (all candidates, no recommendation) or
  curated (approved records plus an attributed release selection) profile.
keywords:
  - thermochemistry
  - chemical kinetics
  - computational chemistry
  - scientific database
  - provenance
  - data curation
license: MIT
